<Base title="Local AI document tools · dropkit" description="A local AI workflow project for reports, meeting notes, and translation: purpose, scope, and setup.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Public project · documentation snapshot · 2026-09-22</p><h1>Local AI document tools</h1>
  <p>A local-first, draft-first UI-to-document automation framework. It defines bounded adapter contracts for local files, foreign-language material, browser or native-surface observations, and local program integrations, then produces one evidence-linked DOCX, XLSX, or PPTX draft when a matching adapter is supplied.</p>
  <h2>What does it do?</h2><p>The public README describes a workflow that combines task settings with locally processed material to produce Word documents.</p>
  <ul><li>Reports and meeting notes</li><li>Foreign-language translation and documentation</li><li>Browser, native-app, and local-program adapter boundaries</li></ul>
  <h2>Working approach</h2><p>I define the task and desired output, inspect the result, and decide what is published.</p>
  <h2>Current verification scope</h2><p>This page summarizes the public README and workflow contract as of September 22, 2026. The Windows download is the engine release lane; the experimental harness and SDK are source-level framework work and are not included in that ZIP. This page does not claim independently reproduced real-host runs, quality or speed measurements, or user acceptance.</p>
  <p>See the repository for requirements and current setup instructions. The same code repository contains an experimental <a href="https://github.com/Hskim-droid/local-llm/tree/db39e7dd4f1d0e54007995efc22771d9fb1c571a/agent-harness">UI-to-document harness</a> with a thin SDK for adapter-supplied, draft-first workflows. The <a href="https://github.com/Hskim-droid/local-llm/blob/db39e7dd4f1d0e54007995efc22771d9fb1c571a/docs/WORKFLOW_CONTRACT.md">workflow contract</a> defines the input adapters, provenance checks, local translation boundary, and one-artifact output rule. Real ERP/QMS, mail, transcription, and host-permission integrations remain unverified.</p>
